        ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)={({x}^{5}-7{x}^{4})}^{2},$ find ${f}^{\u2032}(x).$\n\n${f}^{\u2032}(x)=2({x}^{5}-7{x}^{4})($\n{{field-1}}\n$)$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $g(x)={x}^{5}-7{x}^{4}$ and $f(g(x))=g(x)^{2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(g(x)) & =({g}^{2})^{\u2032}=2g, \\\\ {g}^{\u2032}(x) & =({x}^{5}-7{x}^{4})^{\u2032}=5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & ={f}^{\u2032}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(x) \\\\  & =2g\\cdot (5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =2({x}^{5}-7{x}^{4})(\\,5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
