        ":question/id": "97e8ab80-425a-5ce3-aeca-1b6c32080f6d",
        ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=\\sqrt{5x-3},$ find ${f}^{\u2032}(x).$\n\n${f}^{\u2032}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $g(x)=5x-3$ and $f(g(x))=\\sqrt{g(x)}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(g(x)) & ={(\\sqrt{g})}^{\u2032}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}}, \\\\ {g}^{\u2032}(x) & =(5x-3)^{\u2032}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & ={f}^{\u2032}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
